    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup heavily leveraged against the favorable matchup provided by Mikolas. **Trea Turner** (77.49) and **Kyle Schwarber** (74.47) lead the offensive charge, capitalizing on the generous 4.77 xERA of the opposing starter. While **Kyle Schwarber** carries a slight penalty for historical BvP struggles, both he and **Trea Turner** gain massive utility from their leadoff positioning and the favorable park factors. **Kazuma Okamoto** (67.88) also stands out as a high-floor play, leveraging a strong platoon advantage against Peterson to secure his spot as our premier UTIL option. The priority for today remains stolen base accumulation, with **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.03) remaining a core start despite facing the high-level talent of Cease; his dynamic platoon edge and speed profile necessitate his presence in the outfield.\n\nOur most difficult bench decision involved **Carson Benge** (41.68), who just missed the cut against a 3.80 xERA arm. Despite a respectable projected output, the combination of a difficult left-on-left platoon scenario and the high efficiency scores of our middle infield corps forced him to the pine to protect our daily game caps. Conversely, **Hector Rodriguez** (55.61) narrowly held onto his starting spot, as his elite 0.578 xwOBA profile provides a high-upside swing factor that **Gary Sanchez** (37.54) and **Dillon Dingler** (34.23) simply could not match, as both fell well below our 40.0 efficiency floor. \n\nRisk management for this rotation centers on the volatility of facing elite arms like Miller and Cease. While **Colt Keith** (45.29) and **Christian Yelich** (52.10) are active, their scores are suppressed by the SP skill disadvantage of their respective matchups. **Christian Yelich** in particular faces a tight window where the speed of his catching opposition may neutralize his base-stealing impact. We will monitor the weather reports for the Miller start to ensure **Colt Keith** remains viable, but for now, the Zebras are positioned to maximize efficiency across all five categories.",
